  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 4c1c9e7d653802d17a2ac1687849a654, type: 3}
  m_Name: StudyDefinition
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::Meowra.Data.StudyDefinition
  consentText: "CONSENT TO PARTICIPATE IN RESEARCH\nCompiler Feedback Study\n\nPlease read this information before deciding whether to participate. You may ask the researcher questions before you begin.\n\nKEY INFORMATION\nYou are invited to take part in research about how people experience different styles of programming-error feedback. Participation is voluntary and is expected to take approximately 12\u201318 minutes, depending on your reading speed. We expect little risk, mainly temporary frustration or tiredness. There is no expected direct benefit to you and no payment for participating. Your responses may contribute to scientific understanding of programming support tools. You may choose not to participate or stop at any time without penalty or loss of benefits to which you are otherwise entitled.\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\nYou will read brief instructions, review six short programming-error scenarios presented with different feedback styles, and select an answer for each scenario. After each pair of scenarios, you will answer a short questionnaire about the feedback. You will also answer questions about your experience with the assistant, choose a preferred feedback style, and have an opportunity to explain your preference in your own words. The feedback is prepared in advance; the study does not send your responses to a live AI service.\n\nRISKS AND DISCOMFORTS\nThe activities are expected to involve risks similar to ordinary computer-based reading and problem solving. You may experience mild frustration, boredom, fatigue, or eye strain. There is also a possible risk of loss of privacy if research records are accessed without authorization. You may pause or stop if you feel uncomfortable. Tell the researcher if you have a concern or experience a problem.\n\nBENEFITS AND PAYMENT\nYou should not expect a personal benefit, payment, or other reward. The possible benefit is contributing to research on how programming feedback is presented and experienced.\n\nYOUR CHOICE\nTaking part is your choice. You may decline by selecting the return-to-setup button instead of Accept. You may stop later by telling the researcher or closing the study. Some questions require an answer to advance; if you do not want to answer, you may stop rather than continue. You do not have to give a reason. Responses already submitted are saved as you go.\n\nINFORMATION RECORDED AND PRIVACY\nThe app assigns a random participant ID and does not ask for your name. It records the assigned feedback and task order, your selected answers, whether each answer is correct, time spent on each programming question, questionnaire ratings, your preferred feedback style, and any written explanation you provide. It also records your consent decision and its time. Please do not include your name or other identifying details in written responses.\n\nRecords are saved locally on the study computer. The app does not automatically upload them. A random ID reduces identification risk but does not guarantee complete anonymity, especially if you include identifying information in a written response.\n\n[RESEARCHER TO COMPLETE: Who may access the records, how they will be protected, how long they will be retained, and whether individual-level data or quotations will be shared or used in future research.]\n\n[RESEARCHER TO COMPLETE: Whether already-submitted responses will be retained if you stop, and how and until when you can request their removal. Because the app does not collect your name, locating a record later may require its participant ID.]\n\nQUESTIONS AND CONTACTS\nFor questions about the study, or to report a study-related problem or harm, contact:\n[RESEARCHER NAME, INSTITUTION, AND EMAIL OR PHONE]\n\nFor questions about your rights as a research participant, or concerns you prefer to discuss with someone independent of the study team, contact:\n[INSTITUTIONAL IRB / RESEARCH ETHICS OFFICE AND EMAIL OR PHONE]\n\nYOUR CONSENT\nBy selecting Accept, you indicate that you have read this information, have had an opportunity to ask questions, and voluntarily agree to participate. Selecting Accept does not waive any of your legal rights. If you do not wish to participate, do not select Accept."
  scenarios:
  - {fileID: 11400000, guid: fb147655216905c0aa17dbd70a8cf0d8, type: 2}
