  - {fileID: 11400000, guid: b6af74c816ccd62f5aa0748d7d92a7ad, type: 2}
  meowraPortrait: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 32f6bc7430c81fdc7913e9cb77c6fdd6, type: 3}
  meowraIntroduction: "Alright, now it's my turn to help you with the errors, nya! I'll explain what each error means and offer a hint to help you work through it. Take your time—we'll tackle this together."
  consentQuote: "Nya! This page explains what taking part involves and the risks associated with the experiment. Please read it before deciding whether to participate."
  hostIntroduction: "Hi, I'm Dr. Meowra, your catgirl assistant! I'm here to guide you through this coding assignment, nya. Don't worry about getting everything right—we'll take it one step at a time. I'll stay with you throughout the study, and in my feedback block I'll help explain the coding errors. Paws ready?"
  hostQuote: "Paws ready! The researcher can choose the session settings here."
  surveyQuote: "That's the first pair of tasks finished. How did that feedback style feel to use?"
  completionQuote: "Meowtastic effort! Thank you for taking part, purrr!"
  answerEncouragements:
  - "One question at a time, nya. Take the time you need!"
  - "I'm here with you, nya. Give this question your best try!"
  - "Keep going at your own pace. You've got this, meow!"
  - "Paws up for sticking with it! Take a moment to think."
  - "No rush, nya. Give yourself time to work through this question."
  - "One last coding question, nya. Keep giving it your best!"
  hostIntroductionQuote: "A little hello before we begin, nya. Let me introduce myself!"
  instructionsQuote: "Let me show you what to do. We'll take it one question at a time, nya!"
  blockIntroductionQuote: "My explanation block is coming up, meow. Here's what to expect."
  secondEvaluationQuote: "Two blocks down, nya. Please rate the style you just experienced."
  thirdEvaluationQuote: "You've tried all three styles. These ratings are for the most recent block."
  personaMeasuresQuote: "This page asks about your experience with me. Candid answers are welcome, nya."
  preferenceQuote: "Looking back at the three styles, which would you choose to use?"
  openResponseQuote: "I'd like to hear your reasons in your own words. Share whatever stood out to you."
